From e93707933f89da8b51a7c812f089904220fcac68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:17:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FieldOperations: parallel algorithms of C++, tests with nvc++
 -stdpar=gpu

The MGIS/FieldOperations/ParallelSTLFieldOperations.hxx header copies and
fills views with the parallel algorithms of the C++ standard library. It
is the counterpart of the stlpar backend of the generic-parallel interface:
the algorithms run on the host with gcc, clang or icpx (in parallel with
libstdc++ only if TBB is found and linked), and on an NVIDIA GPU with
nvc++ -stdpar=gpu. A copy between two views with the same dense layout is a
std::copy, the other copies and the fills call a function object per point
over a counting iterator of its own (std::views::iota makes the algorithms
of libstdc++ run sequentially). The type of the execution policy is a
template parameter (parallel_unsequenced_policy by default), deduced from
the policy given to the constructor. The standard only guarantees the
global objects of the policies: the default constructor uses them, and a
policy that can't be copied (as with libc++) is kept by reference. The
header compiles with gcc, nvc++, clang with libstdc++ and clang with libc++.

Tests: the body of FieldOperationsCUDATest moves to FieldOperationsTest.hxx,
written for a backend described by the FieldOperationsTestBackend concept
(location of the arrays, shared memory, arrays, operations, policies,
synchronizations, tolerance of the stresses of the cycle). Every check of
the CUDA test is kept; the two checks that only concern a device (mixed
copy, mass density held on the host) are only made for a backend whose
arrays are in the memory of a device. The stresses of the cycle are checked
within 1e-12 for cuda and for the host, 1e-11 for nvc++ (difference
measured: 1.2e-12). A failure of cudaStreamDestroy fails the CUDA test, as
before. Since the body is now also compiled by the C++ compiler of MGIS,
its warnings (-Wshadow, -Wfloat-equal) are fixed.

- FieldOperationsParallelSTLTest: the same checks with the stlpar backend
  on the host, always built with the generic-parallel tests, and the
  copies and fills with the par, seq and unseq policies.
- enable-generic-parallel-stlpar-nvhpc-gpu-tests (OFF by default, CMake
  3.20): libraries generated with the stlpar backend and compiled by
  nvc++ -stdpar=gpu for an NVIDIA GPU (the libraries of the cuda tests),
  GenericParallelCUDATest compiled by nvc++ for them
  (GenericParallelNVHPCGPUTest) and FieldOperationsParallelSTLTest compiled
  by nvc++ (FieldOperationsParallelSTLNVHPCGPUTest, arrays in the memory of
  the device only). nvc++ is given by MGIS_NVHPC_CXX_COMPILER, its options
  by MGIS_NVHPC_GPU_FLAGS, whatever the C++ compiler of MGIS. Each source
  is compiled by a custom command, the libraries are described by imported
  targets. The objects and the tests depend on the headers they include
  (DEPFILE) and on the options, the libraries have a run path to the
  libraries of TFEL.

In float, the Norton behaviour compiled by nvc++ differs from the
reference by 3.1e-5 on the stresses and 1.5e-3 on the tangent operator at
the onset of the flow, on the GPU as on the host (-stdpar=multicore) and
without contraction (-gpu=nofma): the float tolerances of
GenericParallelCUDATest depend on the compiler (5e-5 and 3e-3 for nvc++,
unchanged for nvcc). The tests pass in double and in float.

The sources generated by MFront now depend on the configuration file of
the backend, which is only written when it changes: the libraries are
generated again when the options of the backend change.

Documentation: views, installation, release notes.
