+### Tests of the `generic-parallel` interface with `nvc++ -stdpar=gpu`
+
+The `enable-generic-parallel-stlpar-nvhpc-gpu-tests` option enables the
+same tests for the behaviours, models and material properties generated
+with the `stlpar` backend and compiled by `nvc++ -stdpar=gpu` for an
+`NVIDIA` GPU, and the field operations of the parallel algorithms on the
+GPU (`ParallelSTLFieldOperations`). The libraries and the tests are
+compiled by `nvc++` (variable `MGIS_NVHPC_CXX_COMPILER`, options given by
+the `MGIS_NVHPC_GPU_FLAGS` variable), whatever the `C++` compiler of
+`MGIS`. Those tests require an `NVIDIA` GPU, the `NVIDIA` HPC SDK,
+`cmake` 3.20 or later and a `TFEL` providing the `generic-parallel`
+interface. `OFF` by default.
+
 ### HDF5 support
 
 The following options control the support of the `HDF5` library:
